      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T04:30:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tend to agree with Chiachang that this is confusing – case in point.\n\nThe issue here is that you are calling a method whose return value depends on the current contents of a state member. That\u0027s what\u0027s confusing here, and it\u0027s a common antipattern.\n\nThe standard solution to this is to pass the configuration object to isTetherProvisioningRequired (you don\u0027t have to pass mSystemProperties as this does not contain state changing over the lifetime of EntitlementManager). The change is trivial because in all other places you can just pass mConfig.\n\nThat will also let you use the local instead of the member throughout in this function for cleanliness.\n\nIdeally, I think this change should be preceded by a cleanup where you add the finals and the nullability annotations, the log cleanups, the cleanup to updateEntitlementCacheValue and change isTetherProvisioningRequired to take a config object.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "2adff45ce493db10235823b041e1d6d60da51888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01292c71_3d638dc8",
