    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b9e84c8_9cc40991",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/tethering/EntitlementManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T04:30:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this looks a bit dangerous to me. I understand the premise, but maybe we need some kind of timeout or something ?\n\nThere are many provisioning apps and we don\u0027t control them ; we should expect some of them to have bugs. Here is the kind of scenario I\u0027m concerned about :\n\n- User enables tethering to mobile.\n- Tethering starts running the silent provisioning flow.\n- The provisioning app has a temporary problem and crashes before it sends the broadcast. Or, the device is under extreme memory pressure and it\u0027s killed by the system before it can send the broadcast.\n- Tethering doesn\u0027t start (that\u0027s not different than before and is unavoidable if the entitlement app crashes, so that\u0027s fine here)\n- Even after the device has recovered, now trying to enable tethering doesn\u0027t do anything until you reboot the device.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 288,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 288,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "2adff45ce493db10235823b041e1d6d60da51888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
